<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ ADRs close steady in N.Y., Dow drops 57 points.</title>
<headline>NZ ADRs close steady in N.Y., Dow drops 57 points.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs closed steady to slightly stronger in the U.S. while the Dow dropped 57.40 points to end at 6,820.28.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S., Britain and Australia.</p>
<p>Company		   Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>Tranz Rail		  N.Y.     US$18	     nil</p>
<p>FCL Bldg		    N.Y.     US$30	     +0 1/8</p>
<p>FCL Engy		    N.Y.     US$26 5/8	 +0 1/4</p>
<p>FCL Paper		   N.Y.     US$19 5/8	 nil</p>
<p>FCL Forest		  N.Y.     US$12 3/4	 nil</p>
<p>Telecom		     N.Y.     US$71 1/8	 +1</p>
<p>Thislte		     London   178 1/2	   -4 1/2</p>
<p>Guinness Peat	     London   36		  -0 1/2</p>
<p>Brierley		    London   untraded</p>
<p>NZ IT			 London   244		 nil</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col	     London   158 1/4	   -3</p>
<p>Templeton		   London   144 1/2	   +2 1/2</p>
<p>Lion			  Sydney   A$2.98		n/a</p>
<p>Goodman		     Sydney   A$1.62		n/a</p>
<p>Macraes		     Sydney   A$2.39		n/a</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of 16 shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
